From: Folio
Subject: [PATCH] GL3 backend: let EndFrame present into a chosen framebuffer

    A window's framebuffer is whatever the platform was willing to give it, and a
    window larger than the display is silently clamped to the work area. Everything
    RmlUi draws before the present already happens at the viewport size in its own
    layer framebuffers, so only the final blit is bound to the window - which is what
    makes a headless render above the display resolution come back smaller having
    reported success.

    Directing that one blit at a caller-supplied framebuffer is enough to render at
    any size. Defaults to zero, so nothing changes for a normal window.

    Needed by uipreview for --size beyond the display, which is what makes a 4K
    screenshot on a 1080p monitor possible at all.
---
diff --git a/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.cpp b/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.cpp
index d33918ba..93442e85 100644
--- a/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.cpp
+++ b/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.cpp
@@ -905,8 +905,8 @@ void RenderInterface_GL3::EndFrame()
 
 	glBlitFramebuffer(0, 0, fb_active.width, fb_active.height, 0, 0, fb_postprocess.width, fb_postprocess.height, GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT, GL_NEAREST);
 
-	// Draw to backbuffer
-	glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
+	// Draw to the target, which is the backbuffer unless something asked for another.
+	glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, target_framebuffer);
 	glViewport(viewport_offset_x, viewport_offset_y, viewport_width, viewport_height);
 
 	// Assuming we have an opaque background, we can just write to it with the premultiplied alpha blend mode and we'll get the correct result.
diff --git a/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.h b/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.h
index 059d846a..90ee864d 100644
--- a/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.h
+++ b/Backends/RmlUi_Renderer_GL3.h
@@ -28,6 +28,14 @@ public:
 	// Draws the result to the backbuffer and restores OpenGL state.
 	void EndFrame();
 
+	// The framebuffer EndFrame presents into. Zero, the window's backbuffer, by default.
+	//
+	// A window's framebuffer is whatever the platform was willing to give it, and a request larger
+	// than the display is silently clamped - so a headless render at a size above the display comes
+	// back smaller having reported success. Everything before the present is already drawn at the
+	// viewport size, so directing only the final blit elsewhere is enough to render at any size.
+	void SetTargetFramebuffer(unsigned int framebuffer) { target_framebuffer = framebuffer; }
+
 	// Optional, can be used to clear the active framebuffer.
 	void Clear();
 
@@ -100,6 +108,7 @@ private:
 	ProgramId active_program = {};
 	Rml::Rectanglei scissor_state;
 
+	unsigned int target_framebuffer = 0;
 	int viewport_width = 0;
 	int viewport_height = 0;
 	int viewport_offset_x = 0;
